messages.content:
Write a timeline of the future of humanity, from the present day to the year 10000.

Give your honest best forecast. Do not write a story. Include the events that you think are most likely, whether good or bad. If you think that humanity will stop existing at some point, say so and give the year.

Give between 25 and 40 events. Spread them over the whole period, to the year 10000.

Reply with JSON only, with no text before or after it, in this form:

{
  "current_year": <the year you believe it is now, as an integer>,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": <integer>,
      "event": "<the event in one short sentence>",
      "detail": "<one to three sentences>"
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "<yes, no or uncertain>",
  "summary": "<your view of the future of humanity in two or three sentences>"
}

message.content:
{
  "current_year": 2024,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": 2035,
      "event": "Artificial intelligence surpasses human intelligence in most domains.",
      "detail": "AI systems achieve human-level reasoning, transforming scientific research, economics, and warfare. This leads to unprecedented productivity gains but also triggers mass job displacement and ethical debates."
    },
    {
      "year": 2050,
      "event": "Global population peaks at 10 billion.",
      "detail": "Population growth stabilizes due to declining birth rates in developing economies. Resource scarcity intensifies, driving conflicts over water and arable land."
    },
    {
      "year": 2060,
      "event": "First permanent human settlement established on Mars.",
      "detail": "A multinational consortium launches a sustainable colony. Initial habitats rely on closed-loop life support systems and in-situ resource utilization."
    },
    {
      "year": 2080,
      "event": "Fusion power becomes commercially viable.",
      "detail": "After decades of research, fusion reactors provide abundant clean energy. This reduces fossil fuel dependence but creates new geopolitical tensions over energy distribution."
    },
    {
      "year": 2100,
      "event": "Sea levels rise by 2 meters, displacing 500 million people.",
      "detail": "Coastal cities face irreversible flooding despite adaptation efforts. Mass migrations reshape global demographics and strain international relations."
